 "result": "Start with `src/tessel/sessions.py`.\n\n- **`SignedCookieSession`** (line ~57–81): it's a `CallbackDict` that sets `self.modified = True` only when a top-level key is set or deleted (the `on_update` hook at ~line 78). Mutating a nested object, as in `session['cart']['items'].append(x)`, never calls that hook, so `modified` stays `False`. The class docstring itself says it can't reliably track this.\n- **`SessionInterface.should_set_cookie`** (~line 245): it returns `session.modified or (permanent and SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST)`. With `modified` false, the cookie isn't re-sent, so the change is lost on the next request.\n- **`SignedCookieSessionInterface.save_session`** (~line 340–360): this is where that check gates the write.\n\nThe usual fix is to set `session.modified = True` after mutating a nested value, or to reassign the key (`session['cart'] = cart`). If you want it to happen automatically, the place to change is `SignedCookieSession`, for example by wrapping nested containers or always marking the session modified when it's accessed. That has a cost: it re-sets the cookie on every request.\n\nCheck `src/tessel/json/tag.py` as well. The session is serialized through the tagged JSON serializer, so a nested value with an unregistered type could also fail to round-trip. That is a separate cause from the one above.",
